{"success": true, "name": "arc-demo-grounding", "file": "references/rejection-audit-and-demo-selection.md", "content": "# Rejection audit and choosing the next demo

An incorrect ARC submission is binary feedback; it does not reveal which assumption failed. After rejection, rebuild the candidate from the original grid and audit the entire pipeline:

- input segmentation and object boundaries;
- which objects or regions are selected, including negative examples;
- output dimensions and coordinate/order mapping;
- transformation scope and fill/color semantics;
- cells that should remain unchanged, including possible changes to scaffold or background;
- exact transcription and serialization.

Compare the complete changed-cell mask of each demo, not just the visually salient interiors. If multiple rules still fit, write down how they differ on the test and request an example likely to distinguish them. Do not spend submissions on speculative local edits to a rejected grid. Weigh the fixed demo cost against remaining attempts and uncertainty.

This is a general reassessment procedure, not a claim about any particular ARC transformation.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792544721/attempts/cad7481303e4469588333dc46b5ca8fd/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/arc-demo-grounding/references/rejection-audit-and-demo-selection.md"}

